<HelpChapterSection Id="faq">
    <HelpTopicSection Id="faq-common">
        <div class="help-faq">
            <details>
                <summary>How do I get access to KOD?</summary>
                <div><p>There is no self-registration. Contact the HR department or the system administrator — they will create an account for you and give you a temporary password. Then see “<a href="/help#account-first-login">Signing in for the first time</a>”.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>The authenticator code is not accepted.</summary>
                <div>
                    <p>The most common reasons:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>the time on your phone is inaccurate — turn on automatic date and time;</li>
                        <li>the code has already been used — each code works once, wait for the next one (up to 30 seconds);</li>
                        <li>the app has several “KOD” entries — use the newest one (after setting up the authenticator again, the old entries can be deleted).</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>If nothing helps, sign in with a recovery code and ask the administrator to reset your authenticator.</p>
                </div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>I lost my phone or deleted the authenticator app.</summary>
                <div><p>Sign in with a recovery code (<span class="help-ui">Sign in with a recovery code</span> on the code page) and ask the administrator to reset your authenticator. If you have no recovery codes, contact the administrator right away. After the reset, you will set up the new phone when you sign in.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Why was I signed out of the cabinet?</summary>
                <div>
                    <ul>
                        <li>an hour passed without activity or 12 hours since sign-in — this is a security limit, just sign in again;</li>
                        <li>you closed the browser and didn't check “Remember me on this device” when signing in;</li>
                        <li>you changed your password or clicked <span class="help-ui">Sign out on other devices</span> on another device — the sign-ins on the other devices end within a few minutes;</li>
                        <li>an administrator blocked the account, issued a temporary password, reset the authenticator or signed out all your sessions.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>A module I need is missing from the menu.</summary>
                <div><p>The menu shows only the modules you have permissions for. Check your permissions in <span class="help-ui">Profile</span> → <span class="help-ui">All my permissions</span> and contact the head of your unit or the administrator. Changes to permissions take effect within 5 minutes at most, without signing in again.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>My document was rejected. What should I do?</summary>
                <div><p>Open the document, read the reason in the signing route, click <span class="help-ui">Edit</span>, correct the file, the details or the route, and click <span class="help-ui">Save and send for signing</span>. Those who have already signed the current file don't sign again; if you replace the file, everyone will have to sign it. Details — “<a href="/help#documents-edit">Editing a draft or a rejected document</a>”.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Can I change a document that is already in signing?</summary>
                <div><p>As long as nobody has signed it, the author can click <span class="help-ui">Withdraw</span> — the document returns to drafts and can be edited. If someone has already signed it, the document can be changed only after one of the signers declines.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Is my key or key password sent to the server?</summary>
                <div><p>No. The key is read only in your browser, in a separate protected thread, and is released from memory right after signing. Only the finished signature (for documents) and service requests to the provider reach the server: the certificate status check and the timestamp (only a hash of the data).</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Which signature format should I choose?</summary>
                <div><p>Unless the recipient requires something else — <strong>CAdES</strong>, level <strong>B-LT</strong>. For a PDF that must open in a regular viewer — <strong>PAdES</strong>. Details — “<a href="/help#signing-formats">Signature formats and levels</a>”.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>My key is on a token (Almaz, Crystal) or in the cloud (Diia.Signature). Can I sign?</summary>
                <div><p>Not yet: KOD supports file keys (Key-6.dat, PFX, JKS, etc.). Most providers, including Diia and the State Tax Service, also issue file keys free of charge.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Can I sign a document from my phone?</summary>
                <div><p>Yes, if the key file is on your phone: the interface fully works on mobile devices. Signing is done in the browser the same way as on a computer.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>How do I print or save this manual?</summary>
                <div><p>Click <span class="help-ui">Print / PDF</span> at the top of the page and choose a printer or “Save as PDF”. Each chapter starts on a new page.</p></div>
            </details>
        </div>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="faq-support">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account, full name, positions, forgotten password</strong> — the HR department.</li>
            <li><strong>Access to modules, authenticator reset, blocking, technical problems</strong> — the system administrator.</li>
            <li><strong>Signing route, document content, declined signing</strong> — the author of the document.</li>
            <li><strong>Electronic signature key, its password, validity period, revocation</strong> — your trust service provider (for example, the State Tax Service, Diia or a bank). KOD does not store and cannot recover your key.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>When reporting a problem, include: what you were doing, the exact text of the message, the time and the browser. Important actions are recorded in the audit log, so the administrator can quickly find the event.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>
</HelpChapterSection>
